> Would you recommend using the ULS or the ULSMV estimator?

I think for ordinal data "ulsmv" is a better option than "uls". and if your sample size is not low, "wlsmv" is better than "ulsmv" but you can compare results for both methods and if they are the same you can use wlsmv.

The performance of ML, DWLS, and ULS estimation with robust corrections in structural equation models with ordinal variables - PubMed <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27571021/>
Robust/scaled statistics in CFA on ordinal response data <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/DlVaoP41MyI?pli=1>
outliers - Robustification in lavaan: Difference between M, MV and MVS? - Cross Validated <https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/608503/robustification-in-lavaan-difference-between-m-mv-and-mvs>
(PDF) A comparison among robust estimation methods for structural equations modeling with ordinal categorical variables <https://www.researchgate.net/publication/349337902_A_comparison_among_robust_estimation_methods_for_structural_equations_modeling_with_ordinal_categorical_variables?enrichId=rgreq-904dbc7eee89d141b15248ec27e59b0f-XXX&enrichSource=Y292ZXJQYWdlOzM0OTMzNzkwMjtBUzo5OTE3NDY1OTA3ODE0NDFAMTYxMzQ2MjIyMTI4NA%3D%3D&el=1_x_3&_esc=publicationCoverPdf>

